WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.880
- So, the tour is for
your album "Gaslighter".

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.678
A lot of people relate to
this album and the message and

00:00:06.678 --> 00:00:10.420
and just, I guess from an
artist's point of view, like,

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.670
how hard is it, asking for a friend

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:17.300
while I'm currently writing,
through a similar situation is

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.643
how hard is that to write so openly?

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:23.830
And so honest, while navigating children,

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.870
while navigating people, you know,

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:28.040
you're under a microscope.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:28.873
Like there's so much, like,

00:00:28.873 --> 00:00:30.690
I feel like I've written
so many songs myself,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.630
for my personal like life,

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.660
and I keep kind of going,
ooh, should I do that?

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.630
Or, oh God. Or is that?
Did you go through that?

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:39.270
Like while writing this?

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.507
- I definitely wanted to be very blatant

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.990
and like literal with this one.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:48.280
But yeah, I was still, I wasn't
like beyond all the emotion

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.260
like I am now.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.920
And then there's a stress of, oh my gosh,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.728
now my kids are gonna hear this. And then.

00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:53.731
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:53.731 --> 00:00:54.570
- Now my son is on tour with us.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.941
He's in the band and I'm
like, this is kinda weird.

00:00:56.941 --> 00:00:58.931
(everyone laughing)

00:00:58.931 --> 00:01:02.808
I'm always checking, are
you okay? Are you all right?

00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:05.320
- Oh my God, I know, 'cause
that could be awkward.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:06.370
- [Natalie] Yeah.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.580
- But I love the fact
that, like, he's an artist,

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.720
so he does get the fact that like,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.089
it's very therapeutic for us
to like, that's our outlet.

00:01:13.089 --> 00:01:14.310
- There's no way around it.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.780
When you write falsely, it doesn't work.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:18.400
- [Kelly] It's transparent
that you're full of crap, yeah.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.610
- You have to be, yeah,
you have to be real.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.510
- Agreed. Sorry, I was so blunt.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.970
- It's weird. The more specific you are,

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.306
the more it's universal to other people.

00:01:26.306 --> 00:01:28.856
- Which isn't that so sad?

00:01:28.856 --> 00:01:30.040
- Yeah. I know.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.950
- I mean life is so hard. Yeah.
It's sad that people relate.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.100
Okay, so we all went through divorces.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:41.090
And how did you each find
strength? And not just music,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.370
I think it's therapeutic, but
like your female friendships,

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.670
I feel like that has really helped me.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:48.660
- Yeah. I remember when you
first came down in the studio

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.243
in Nashville and said

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.740
guys, I just wanna tell
you I'm getting a divorce.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.900
- Which time was this?

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.990
(everyone laughing)

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:57.823
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:57.823 --> 00:01:59.943
- The first one. Number one.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.790
I remember thinking, well,
I'm getting a divorce.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.450
Now she's said she's getting a divorce.

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.030
Now I can't say I'm getting a divorce.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:08.576
It was kind, but then I was like.

00:02:08.576 --> 00:02:10.179
- But me saying it, 'cause
you were keeping it?

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:11.080
- I hadn't told y'all! I was keeping,

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.293
I was feeling like
everybody was gonna judge me

00:02:13.293 --> 00:02:14.520
'cause I was like,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.730
I thought I was first getting the divorce.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.480
- [Kelly] You kept that in?

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.313
- Yeah.

00:02:18.313 --> 00:02:20.662
- So I was like, guys,
I'm getting a divorce.

00:02:20.662 --> 00:02:21.666
And Martie's like.

00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:22.733
- Me too!

00:02:22.733 --> 00:02:23.891
- I'm having a horrible marriage!

00:02:23.891 --> 00:02:25.357
- Oh my gosh!

00:02:25.357 --> 00:02:28.160
- Well this was great 'cause I felt,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.380
'cause I didn't know anybody close to me

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.370
that was getting a divorce.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.400
So it was, I was so happy for you.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.013
- I know. Wait, we were divorce buddies.

